      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a potent signalling molecule that directly activates the mTOR pathway, sensing sufficient amino acid availability to encourage muscle growth. By stimulating mTOR, leucine signals the cell to increase protein synthesis above its breakdown rate. A caloric surplus provides the necessary energy substrates, creating positive nitrogen balance by supplying the building blocks for muscle repair and hypertrophy. This surplus ensures the body has excess energy and amino acids to fuel continuous net protein gain.",
